Name":"crays-nostr-article-masthead__meta"},"children":[{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["Relays"]},{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["8 min read"]},{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["Source inventory"]}]},"\n              ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{"className":"crays-nostr-article-masthead__title"},"children":["Research Source: sesseor raw relay list"]},"\n              ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{"className":"crays-nostr-article-masthead__deck"},"children":["Research Source: sesseor raw relay list in the relay layer: storage, discovery, access, policy, uptime and the boring server details that decide whether Nostr feels alive."]},"\n            "]},"\n\n            ",{"tag":"div","attributes":{"className":"crays-nostr-reader-note"},"children":[{"tag":"strong","attributes":{},"children":["The quick read"]},{"tag":"span","attributes":{},"children":["Research Source: sesseor raw relay list in the relay layer: storage, discovery, access, policy, uptime and the boring server details that decide whether Nostr feels alive."]}]},"\n              ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{"id":"relays-are-the-unglamorous-center"},"children":["Relays are the unglamorous center"]},"\n              ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["sesseor raw relay list belongs in Relays because the network feels alive only when events can be stored, found and served. Clients get the screenshots, but relays carry the daily weight."]},"\n              ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["A relay is not just a neutral pipe. It can be public or private, paid or free, strict or loose, fast or exhausted, local or global, archival or temporary. Those choices shape the user experience more than many glossy app pages admit."]},"\n              ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{"id":"discovery-is-a-relay-problem"},"children":["Discovery is a relay problem"]},"\n              ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["If people cannot find your events, portability feels fake. Relay lists, outbox models, search relays, paid relays and app defaults all affect whether a follower actually sees what you publish."]},"\n              ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["sesseor raw relay list should therefore be read as part of discovery, not only infrastructure. The boring server choice becomes a social consequence."]},"\n\n              ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{"id":"policy-lives-close-to-storage"},"children":["Policy lives close to storage"]},"\n              ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Relays choose what to accept, keep, reject, rate-limit or delete. That is not censorship in the old platform sense, but it is still power. Spam, illegal material, harassment, storage bills and local laws do not disappear because the protocol is open."]},"\n              ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["A serious relay article explains the policy surface plainly. Who runs it? What does it store? What does it block? What does it cost? What happens when the operator gets tired?"]},"\n              ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{"id":"the-operator-view"},"children":["The operator view"]},"\n              ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Relay operators need uptime, monitoring, moderation tools, clear limits and a reason to keep paying the bill. Free relays are generous, but generosity is not a business model. Paid relays and community relays exist because server reality eventually knocks on the door."]},"\n              ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Relays matter when a venue, local community, archive or higher-trust room needs public-network identity without losing local usefulness."]},"\n              ",{"tag":"h2","attributes":{"id":"what-to-do-with-it"},"children":["What to do with it"]},"\n              ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["Do not treat sesseor raw relay list as a loose bookmark. Use it as a decision point: which idea does it explain, which page should you read next and which claim needs checking before you repeat it?"]},"\n              ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{},"children":["The useful habit is simple. Read the plain explanation, follow one nearby link and come back with a sharper question. That is how a large Nostr archive turns into a working map instead of a scattered set of browser tabs."]},"\n\n",{"tag":"div","attributes":{"className":"crays-article-end"},"children":["\n              ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"/nostr/"},"children":["Back to the Crays Nostr page"]},"\n            "]},"\n          "]},"\n        "]},"\n      "]},"\n    "]},"\n\n\n\n  ",{"tag":"footer","attributes":{"className":"legal-footer crays-nostr-footer","aria-label":"Crays footer"},"children":["\n    ",{"tag":"div","attributes":{"className":"legal-footer-inner"},"children":["\n      ",{"tag":"div","attributes":{"className":"legal-footer-top"},"children":["\n        ",{"tag":"div","attributes":{},"children":["\n          ",{"tag":"a","attributes":{"className":"legal-footer-logo-link","href":"/","aria-label":"Crays Home"},"children":["\n            ",{"tag":"img","attributes":{"className":"legal-footer-logo","src":"/assets/brand/crays-logo.svg","alt":"Crays","width":"138","height":"34","loading":"lazy"},"children":[]},"\n          "]},"\n          ",{"tag":"p","attributes":{"className":"legal-footer-tagline"},"children":["Luxury, Lifestyle, Wealth and Innovation"]},"\n        "]},"\n        ",{"tag":"div","attributes":{"className":"legal-footer-social","aria-label":"Social links"},"children":[{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"https://github.com/CraysCircle","aria-label":"GitHub","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer noopener"},"children":[{"tag":"img","attributes":{"src":"/assets/footer-icons/github.svg","alt":"GitHub","width":"20","height":"20","loading":"lazy"},"children":[]}]},{"tag":"a","attributes":{"href":"https://x.com/CraysCircle","aria-label":"X","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer noopener"},"children":[{"tag":"img","attributes":{"src":"/assets/footer-icons/x.svg","